Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 MEEI MRN  REMOVED_DATE Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  BARBARA LYNN SMITH  M D  Resident  Russell Ryan  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 40 year old woman with a history of left breast cancer  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  1  RESIDUAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MULTIPLE MICROSCOPIC FOCI RANGING FROM SINGLE CELLS TO REMOVED_DATE CM  IN TOTAL AGGREGATING TO APPROXIMATELY REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO THE INKED MARGIN ALONG A BROAD FRONT   SEE NOTE   2  RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  EXTENSIVE  PRESENT IN 11 OF 13 TISSUE BLOCKS AND PRESENT AT THE INKED MARGIN OF RESECTION IN SEVERAL FOCI AND PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE INKED MARGIN ALONG A BROAD FRONT IN MULTIPLE FOCI  NOTE  The invasive and in situ carcinoma is present in the main  largest  specimen as well as in the smaller tissue fragments submitted in the same container  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm breast excisional biopsy specimen with a needle localization wire passing into one aspect and along the long axis of the specimen  The specimen is unoriented  It is correlated with the specimen radiograph which shows a cylindrical  radiopaque object in the vicinity of the needle localization wire  Also received in the same container are two separate portions of fibrofatty breast tissue  the larger measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm and the other  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  The specimen is serially sectioned perpendicular to the long axis into 10 sections numbered REMOVED_DATE with  1 containing the aspect through which the needle localization wire passed  On cut section  the specimen is primarily fibrous with a 0 5cm diameter  hemorrhagic cavity consistent with biopsy cavity present at one edge margin  sections 3 6   A 0 2cm metal cylinder is found within this cavity in section  6  Two additional fragments of breast tissue are inked blue externally  serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibrofatty breast tissue  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section  1  radial to end margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections  2 9  entire specimen  one per cassette   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section  10  radially to end margin  specimen entirely submitted    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Larger separate fragment  entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Smaller separate fragment  entirely submitted  Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1  Immunohistochemical stains for keratin  p63  calponin and myosin were performed on a representative section of the tumor and confirm the presence of in situ and invasive ductal carcinoma  Addendum  1 by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  report_end  , Absent.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 12 49 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  RESIDUAL INVASIVE CARCINOMA  THREE MICROSCOPIC FOCI  0 1  REMOVED_DATE  AND REMOVED_DATE CM   PRESENT IN THE WALL OF THE BIOPSY CAVITY  SEE NOTE   RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  FOCALLY INVOLVING SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  AND FOCALLY PRESENT AT THE ANTERIOR RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE   Note  Definite blood vascular invasion is not seen  The area of ductal carcinoma in situ that is present at the anterior margin is less than 0 1cm in total size  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO 1 OF 23 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 35                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Lymph Node  Left Axilla   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 30 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are two specimens  Labeled  left breast  short superior  long lateral  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm skin ellipse excised a depth of 0 3cm and containing a 2 5cm well healed linear scar  There is a long stitch designating the lateral aspect  a short stitch designating the superior aspect and a double stitch designating the inferior   deep   margin  The anterior aspect is inked in blue while the posterior is inked in black  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm biopsy cavity with a hemorrhagic  fibrous tract extending to the skin ellipse  There is a firm  tan white  hemorrhagic nodule measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm present in the posterior wall of the biopsy cavity  The cavity is 0 6cm from the posterior inferior margin and 0 6cm from the anterior margin  The rim of stellate fibrosis extends to the posterosuperior and posteroinferior margins  Apparently contiguous with the nodule in the biopsy cavity  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm well circumscribed soft tissue mass with a tan yellow  hemorrhagic rim and brown  variegated center  This nodule is present at the anterior margin and 0 5cm from the posterior margin  Representative sections are taken lateral to medial as follows  SECTION CODE A  Biopsy cavity  nearest  posterior  margin  B  Inferior biopsy cavity  C D  Superior aspect biopsy cavity  E  Fibrous tract to skin from biopsy cavity  F  Inferior aspect biopsy cavity  G  Superior aspect biopsy cavity  H  Hemorrhagic nodule  closest margin anterior  I J  Fibrous areas  Labeled as  left axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of adipose tissue from which multiple lymph nodes are extracted ranging in size from 0 2cm to 1 2cm in greatest dimension  The lymph nodes have been submitted in cassettes K through R  Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION   report_end  , Absent.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  18 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 09 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  1   FORMING TWO NODULES EACH ABOUT REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION IN TISSUE SECTION  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  COMEDO TYPE  INVOLVING MANY DUCTS AND LOBULES IN ALL SECTIONS AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGINS OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel is not seen  The margins appear free of invasive carcinoma  The intra operative macroscopic impression is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 12 05                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 AUG 94 at 07 27 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  firm  yellow tan fibrofatty tissue with a wire and x ray  Inked and sectioned to reveal multiple 0 05cm tan  pale calcifications and fibrosis  Sections with calcifications submitted in cassettes A through C  remaining tissue is submitted entirely in cassettes D through F  Resident  FANG FANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST MASS   NO GROSSLY EVIDENT MALIGNANT TUMOR  O R  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   BREAST MASS   report_end  , Absent.
